    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0379" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.7962/46: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-11T22:00:00-04:00">March 11, 1942—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Your 44, February 25, 11 a.m. For McBride. Details of the credit plan are
                    being worked out and should be available shortly. It is proposed to make Liberia
                    eligible for Lend-Lease aid,<anchor n="14" xml:id="d435-f1"/> which would
                    doubtless cover the needs of the frontier force as described by you. <pb
                        facs="0380" n="368" xml:id="pg368"/> War Department is planning to undertake
                    preliminary road construction to the extent of about $200,000, under the credit,
                    thus relieving Liberia of any immediate responsibility in ordering
                    materials.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
